╭─ Where stored? ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                                                              │
│ ❯ Q1  Where should a session's full transcript, every tool result and each compaction summary be kept once a │
│       run ends? Include the archived sessions, the tool_result records and the full 日本語 transcript, not   │
│       just the latest entry. Assume the developer will often be offline and needs to carry this between      │
│       machines without losing any run history.                                                               │
│                                                                                                              │
│ A ○ SQLite in the repository, beside the worktrees          Preview                                          │
│     One file the checkout can delete, and no service to     ```sql                                           │
│     keep running on any of the machines. Copy it together…    create table if not exists event (             │
│ B ○ Postgres beside the application, shared by every            id integer primary key,                      │
│     machine                                                     session text not null,                       │
│     One more service to run, back up and keep reachable         at text not null,                            │
│     from a laptop that is often offline.                        body json not null                           │
│ C ○ Keep a local log beside each checkout and merge later     ) strict;                                      │
│     Works offline without setting up a server, but syncing  ```                                              │
│     a single run can produce duplicate records.                                                              │
│                                                             A row per event, so the history is the table and │
│                                                             a reader can replay it.                          │
│ ↓ 3 below                                                                                                    │
